{"content":"h15.\n\nMemo-visibility enforcement is duplicated across at least the following distinct server surfaces (each re-implements the PUBLIC/PROTECTED/PRIVATE visibility rule independently rather than delegating to one shared gate):\n\n1. Core gRPC/Connect memo API (single-memo read gate) — `server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:39` (`checkMemoReadAccess`, used by `GetMemo`, comment fetch, etc.)\n2. Core gRPC/Connect memo list query filter (list-time visibility clause) — `server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:218-227` (`VisibilityList` / CEL `visibility in [...]` filter applied in `ListMemos`)\n3. Memo comments service — `server/router/api/v1/memo_service_comments.go:41` and `:148` (checks parent/related memo visibility before allowing comment read/create)\n4. Attachment service (linked-attachment access) — `server/router/api/v1/attachment_service.go:422-451` (`checkAttachmentAccess`)\n5. Memo-attachment endpoints (list/set attachments on a memo) — `server/router/api/v1/memo_attachment_service.go:214-222`\n6. Reaction service — `server/router/api/v1/reaction_service.go:30-38,83`\n7. Mention notification gating — `server/router/api/v1/memo_mention_helpers.go:56-88` (`canUserAccessMentionContext`)\n8. In-app notification payload conversion — `server/router/api/v1/user_service_notifications.go:302-316` (`canViewerAccessMemo`)\n9. Email notification dispatcher — `server/notification/email.go:306-320` (separate `canViewerAccessMemo` implementation, duplicated from #8)\n10. SSE broadcast hub (real-time event fan-out) — `server/router/api/v1/sse_hub.go:134-144` (`canReceive`)\n11. Fileserver / static attachment serving (HTTP, share-token aware) — `server/router/fileserver/fileserver.go:650-704` (`checkAttachmentPermission`)\n12. Frontend sitemap generation — `server/router/frontend/frontend.go:149-151` (hard-filters to `store.Public` only)\n13. User stats aggregation (memo counts/heatmap) — `server/router/api/v1/user_service_stats.go:84-90,218-220`\n\nNotes:\n- Sites #8 and #9 are near-identical duplicate implementations of `canViewerAccessMemo` in two different packages (`server/router/api/v1` vs `server/notification`), which is a concrete instance of the same rule being enforced twice rather than shared.\n- The MCP tool surface (`server/router/mcp/*`) was checked and does not implement its own visibility logic — it proxies to the same v1 API handlers (site #1/#2), so it is not a separate enforcement site.","iteration":19,"turn":1,"type":"assistant"}
